### A book's own accessibility information (EPUB Accessibility metadata).

## Said after the document overview and printed by tw info for an EPUB,
## one fact per line, meaning first. The first line is one of the four
## leads; the details follow when the book gives them. $list is a list of
## terms in words ("table of contents, alternative text"), $text the
## publisher's own words, $name a certifier's name.
access-info-friendly = Barrierefreiheit: laut Verlag für Screenreader geeignet.
access-info-not-text = Barrierefreiheit: laut Verlag lässt sich nicht alles als Text lesen.
access-info-given = Barrierefreiheit: vom Verlag beschrieben.
access-info-none = Keine Angaben zur Barrierefreiheit.
access-info-summary = Zusammenfassung: { $text }.
access-info-modes = Zugriffsarten: { $list }.
access-info-sufficient = Lesbar mit: { $list }.
access-info-features = Funktionen: { $list }.
access-info-hazards = Gefahren: { $list }.
access-info-conformance = Entspricht: { $text }.
access-info-certifier = Zertifiziert von: { $name }.
# Joins two sets of access modes in access-info-sufficient: "text, or text and images".
access-info-or = { $first } oder { $second }
# Joins the access modes inside one set: "text and images".
access-info-and = { $first } und { $second }
